hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18207","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The shade of the believer on the Day of Resurrection is his charity."
"19001","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jaafar, haddathana Shuba from Ata ibn al-Saib from Arfaja who said: I was in a house in which was Utba ibn Farqad, and I wanted to narrate a hadith. He said: And there was a man from among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as though he was more entitled to the hadith than he was. He said: So the man narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: In Ramadan the gates of heaven are opened and the gates of the Fire are closed, and every rebellious devil is chained therein, and a caller calls every night: O seeker of good, come forward, and O seeker of evil, desist."
"19002","Haddathana Ubayda ibn Humayd Abu Abd al-Rahman, haddathani Ata ibn al-Saib from Arfaja who said: I was with Utba ibn Farqad while he was narrating about Ramadan. He said: Then a man from among the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us, and when Utba saw him he was in awe of him and fell silent. He said: So he narrated about Ramadan. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying about Ramadan: In it the gates of the Fire are closed and in it the gates of Paradise are opened and the devils are chained therein. He said: And an angel calls therein: O seeker of good, rejoice; O seeker of evil, refrain, until Ramadan ends."
"22679","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from his father, from a man of the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Al-Sham will be opened for you, and in it is a place called al-Ghutah, meaning Damascus, among the best dwellings of the Muslims, meaning in the great battles."
